<article class="page-prose"><section id="principle" class="prose-section"><h2>Access and reuse</h2><p>Galapagensis connects and interprets documentary evidence held in many places. A description, link or reproduction does not imply ownership of the original, its digital image or the rights attached to it. Public access and permission to reuse are separate matters.</p></section><section id="original" class="prose-section"><h2>Original Galapagensis work</h2><p>Authored texts, research outputs, translations, images and downloadable publications must be used according to their individual rights and licence notices. A licence on one publication does not automatically apply to the rest of the website or to the sources discussed within it.</p><p>Where no reuse licence is stated, do not assume permission to reproduce or adapt protected content. Contact Galapagensis for uses requiring authorization. Applicable copyright exceptions and limitations remain available.</p></section><section id="specification" class="prose-section"><h2>The Technical Specification</h2><p>The Galapagensis Technical Specification, version 1.4, by Edgardo Civallero, is released under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution–NonCommercial–NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0)</a>.</p><p>The licence permits sharing for noncommercial purposes with appropriate attribution and a link to the licence. Modified versions may not be distributed under this licence. For commercial reuse or distribution of adaptations, request separate permission. The licence does not restrict uses permitted by applicable exceptions or limitations.</p><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22816706">Read the specification and its publication notice</a>.</p></section><section id="sources" class="prose-section"><h2>Historical sources and third-party material</h2><p>Photographs, maps, manuscripts, published texts, recordings, specimens and other sources retain their own rights and access conditions. Follow the notice attached to each item and, where relevant, the holding repository’s instructions. Credit the creator and repository as indicated; consult the rights holder when permission is required.</p><p>A source may be in the public domain while a related reproduction or other associated material has separate conditions. Galapagensis does not grant rights it does not hold. A missing or uncertain rights statement is not a declaration of public-domain status.</p></section><section id="voices" class="prose-section"><h2>Contributions, voices and consent</h2><p>Sharing a photograph, document, identification or testimony with Galapagensis does not automatically authorize publication or transfer copyright. Credit, permitted uses, access conditions and any agreed restrictions should be established before publication.</p><p>Oral histories, family material and information about living people require attention to consent, privacy and the conditions under which they were shared. Recordings, transcripts and translations may have different access permissions. Publication does not authorize every subsequent use.</p></section><section id="citation" class="prose-section"><h2>Citation and acknowledgement</h2><p>Cite the author, title, publication date, version where relevant, and DOI or stable URL. For evolving website pages, include the access date and any stated update date. Preserve credits and licence notices when sharing material.</p><p>When using a historical source located through Galapagensis, cite the underlying source and its repository identifier as well as any Galapagensis interpretation on which your work relies. Attribution does not replace permission where permission is required.</p></section><section id="contact" class="prose-section"><h2>Permissions, corrections and concerns</h2><p>For permission requests, identify the item, your intended use, whether it involves adaptation or translation, and its publication context. For a rights or privacy concern, include the page URL and the material concerned so that it can be reviewed.</p><p><a href="mailto:contact@galapagensis.net">contact@galapagensis.net</a></p></section></article></div></section>
